course: dictionary
lesson: 3885
title: Freight: goods on the move
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Freight is a word for goods that are carried from one place to another. Goods are things people buy and sell, such as coal, food, cars or parcels. «A freight train is a long line of wagons pulled by a strong locomotive, carrying coal, containers, cars or stone.» The clues are wagons, locomotive and carrying, so freight means the goods being carried.
explain: Freight can also mean the system of carrying goods, or the money paid for it. Read the words around it. In «air freight», the clue is air: the goods travel by plane. In «by freight», the goods go by transport such as a train or a ship.
explain: Freight can be a verb too. To freight goods means to send them by transport. Try the swap check: "They freighted the coal to the port" means they sent the coal by transport. It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Freight means goods carried by trains, ships, trucks or planes.
fact: Freight can also mean the system of carrying goods, or the money paid for it.
fact: As a verb, freight means to send goods by transport: freight, freights, freighted, freighting.
fact: «Freight train» means a train that carries goods.
fact: In maths problems, freight is often weighed in tonnes.
exercise: «A freight train is a long line of wagons pulled by a strong locomotive.» What is a freight train for? | Carrying passengers to the seaside | Racing other trains on the track | Selling tickets at the station | *Carrying goods
exercise: Maya's dad says the parcels came by air freight. What does this mean? | Passengers flying home for the holidays | Parcels that are very light | *Goods sent by plane | A ticket for a flight
exercise: Tom wrote, "The company freighted the coal to the port by ship." What does freighted mean here? | Dug up from the ground | Counted one by one | Burned for heat | *Sent by transport
test: In maths, freight is often weighed in which unit? | Metres | Seconds | *Tonnes | Litres
test: «The ship will freight the containers across the sea.» What does freight mean here? | *Carry the goods by transport | Stay in the harbour all week | Pay a fine at the harbour | Sail around the island for fun
exam: Which is the best meaning of freight? | A pet that travels with its owner | *Goods carried by trains, ships, trucks or planes | The driver of a lorry | A kind of cheap food sold at markets
